Research on Surface Settlement and Construction Risk
Caused by Shallow-buried Shield Tunnel Construction
in Upper-soft Lower-hard Strata
Abstract: In order to study the surface subsidence character
istics and construction risk control caused by the shallow 
buried shield tunnel construction in upper -soft lower -hard
strata, this paper took the shield construction section of a
drainage reconstruction project in Wuhan as the research ob
ject, and employed the numerical simulation method with fi
nite element software MIDAS-GTS-NX to reveal the surface
subsidence law and construction risk control in such condi
tion. The results showed that in upper-soft lower-hard strata,
as the proportion of rock formations on the tunnel face gradu
ally increases, the maximum surface settlement caused by the
construction of the shield tunnel gradually decreases, the ver
tical displacement of the shield segment top decreases first
and then tends to be stable, and the width of the settlement
tank corresponding to the surface also shows a gradually de
creasing trend; and the shield construction easily causes the
risk of uneven settlement of the surface and the difficulty of
controlling the shield form. Risk control can be carried out by
improving soft soil layers and adjusting shield parameters,
such as shield tunneling speed, shield cutter head speed, jack
thrust, soil cabin pressure, and so forth.
Keywords: upper-soft lower-hard strata; surface subsidence
law; construction risk; parameter control; shield tunneling


